    // toast lands in the top-right corner, 400+ px from the two pin dots it is about, and a repeat
    // press inside the 1.5 s rate limit produced nothing at all - so the conclusion available to a
    // photographer was "the arrow keys are broken in compare". This frame counter pulses BOTH pin
    // labels' borders, which is where the eyes already are.
    let cmp_pin_pulse = Rc::new(Cell::new(0i32));
    // v0.8.126 (judge-first e / audit N26): the bothpin caption is a LINGER, not a permanent
    // fixture. Bothpin is the drag-to-compare entry's default, so an instructional sentence sat
    // over the two photographs indefinitely in the mode whose purpose is looking at them. It shows
